From: Tomonori Nakagawa <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: sprd: pcm-routing: mark the AIF widgets SND_SOC_NOPM

Every frontend and backend AIF widget in sprd-platform-pcm-routing declares
register 0 rather than SND_SOC_NOPM:

  SND_SOC_DAPM_AIF_IN("FE_IF_CAP_DSP_C", "FE_DAI_CAP_DSP_C", 0, 0, 0, 0),
  /*                   wname             stname          wslot wreg ...  */

SND_SOC_NOPM is -1 and snd_soc_dapm_new_widgets() treats any w->reg >= 0 as a
real register to sample for the widget's initial power state. sprd-pcm-routing
is a routing component with no regmap and no .read/.write, so every one of
those reads comes back -EIO and ASoC logs it. On an RG Rotate boot that is 113
error lines before anything else can be read on the panel, which is this
board's only console:

  sprd-pcm-routing sprd-routing-pcm: ASoC error (-5): at
    soc_component_read_no_lock() on sprd-routing-pcm for register: [0x00000000]
   ... 107 of those, plus 2 writes and 4 update_bits

The 75 SND_SOC_DAPM_SWITCH/SWITCH_E widgets in the same table already use
SND_SOC_NOPM and are silent; only the 104 AIF widgets were missed. Nothing
depends on the value that was being read - there is no register behind it -
so this only removes the failed accesses.

Signed-off-by: Tomonori Nakagawa <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
---
